   "evidence": "`grep -n 'golecBiernatWusthoff' Amplitude.lean` yields only the definition (154), `golecBiernatWusthoff_apply_self` (159-161), and the admissibility theorem, which unfolds the constant at lines 179 and 181. By contrast `blackDisc` is fully characterised by `blackDisc_apply_self` (132) and `blackDisc_apply_ne` (136), so no consumer of it needs the body.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/SmallX/Dipole/Amplitude.lean",
   "fix": "Add `golecBiernatWusthoff_def` (or `_apply`) stating `golecBiernatWusthoff Qs x y = 1 - Real.exp (-(Qs ^ 2 / 4 * \u2016x - y\u2016 ^ 2))`, with `:= (rfl)` so consumers do not depend on defeq, plus `@[simp] one_sub_golecBiernatWusthoff : 1 - golecBiernatWusthoff Qs x y = Real.exp (-(Qs ^ 2 / 4 * \u2016x - y\u2016 ^ 2))`, and use them in `isAdmissible_golecBiernatWusthoff` instead of unfolding.",
   "issue": "`golecBiernatWusthoff` has only `golecBiernatWusthoff_apply_self` (line 159). There is no `golecBiernatWusthoff_def`/`_apply` giving the value, and no lemma for its S-matrix `1 - golecBiernatWusthoff Qs x y = Real.exp (-(Qs ^ 2 / 4 * \u2016x - y\u2016 ^ 2))` \u2014 the identity the module docstring advertises as the point of the definition and that the admissibility proof derives inline (lines 176-182, via `simp only [... golecBiernatWusthoff]` and `simp only [golecBiernatWusthoff]`). Any downstream use (the roadmap makes it the standard test initial condition for Layers 2 and 4) must unfold the body or rely on defeq.",
   "line": 154
  }
 ],
